Implement the relay protocol-v1 HANDSHAKE / negotiation on BOTH sides (Swift client in ReluxTunnelCore/RelayProtocol per 2nfz7w; Go relay in relay/ per 3bdplx), using the TASK-260715-2azda7 shared schema/constants and the TASK-260715-111tde binding ADR (hello framing: 12/16-byte hello per the reviewer note) + TASK-260715-18owh7 limits (maxFrame negotiated in [2048,65536] default 4096; other limits fixed/local). IMPLEMENT: the client hello -> relay hello-ack exchange over the SSH exec byte stream (transport-agnostic — consumes the SSHTransport exec channel abstraction; use a test-double byte stream for tests), protocol VERSION negotiation (agree v1 or fail closed on unsupported), maxFrame negotiation (client proposes, relay bounds to its cap, agreed value returned), capability/flags exchange, and fail-closed rejection of malformed/oversized/incompatible hellos with the 18owh7 error codes. Deterministic Swift Testing (client side) + Go tests (relay side) covering: successful negotiation, version mismatch, maxFrame clamping, malformed hello, truncated/oversized hello. Candidate-neutral, transport-agnostic; constants come ONLY from the generated schema (no magic numbers). Build + test via swift build/test (Swift) and the Go test path (relay). Not security testing.


