    38	## Protocol v1
    39	
    40	All integer fields are unsigned and network byte order. An exec session starts
    41	with a handshake, followed by framed messages.
    42	
    43	### Handshake
    44	
    45	Client hello:
    46	
    47	```text
    48	magic[4] = "RLXR"
    49	version:u16 = 1
    50	flags:u16
    51	maxFrame:u32
    52	```
    53	
    54	Server hello:
    55	
    56	```text
    57	magic[4] = "RLXR"
    58	version:u16
    59	status:u16
    60	features:u32
    61	maxFrame:u32
    62	```
    63	
    64	Unknown magic, unsupported version, nonzero status, or an unreasonable frame
    65	limit closes the channel and produces a degraded-mode reason. Version
    66	negotiation never guesses a lower framing format.
    67	
    68	### Envelope
    69	
    70	```text
    71	frameLength:u32
    72	type:u8
    73	flags:u8
    74	associationID:u32
    75	payload[frameLength - 6]
    76	```
    77	
    78	`frameLength` covers `type` through the payload and MUST be between 6 and the
    79	negotiated limit. Reserved flags MUST be zero. Invalid lengths close the relay
    80	session; malformed datagram addresses reject only the association when safe.
    81	
    82	Message types:
    83	
    84	| Value | Name | Direction | Purpose |
    85	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
    86	| `0x10` | `UDP_DATAGRAM` | both | Destination/source address plus UDP payload |
    87	| `0x11` | `UDP_ERROR` | server to client | Bounded error code for an association |
    88	| `0x20` | `PING` | client to server | Health probe with opaque payload |
    89	| `0x21` | `PONG` | server to client | Echoed health response |
    90	| `0x30` | `CLOSE_ASSOCIATION` | both | Release sockets and state for one association |
    91	| `0x31` | `CLOSE_SESSION` | both | Graceful whole-session shutdown |
    92	
    93	### UDP payload
    94	
    95	`UDP_DATAGRAM` reuses the HEV UDP-in-TCP relay layout:
    96	
    97	```text
    98	MSGLEN:u16 | HDRLEN:u8 | ATYP:u8 | DST.ADDR:variable | DST.PORT:u16 | DATA:variable
    99	```
